=== Regression sweep: happy-path tax calc against the live valid row (id=3), wrapped in a
QA-owned outer transaction that was rolled back afterward (DB left byte-identical, read-only).
This exercises the exact nested-SAVEPOINT topology of OrderPlacementService.php (ambient tx
opened at placeOrderTransaction():224, CalculateTaxService called from within it at
placeOrderCore():706) and OrderTaxService.php's storeData:true parcel/prescription branch (:294).
Command: php artisan tinker --execute="DB::beginTransaction(); $result = CalculateTaxService::getCalculatedTax(amount:100.0, productIds:[], taxPayer:'vendor', storeData:true, countryCode:null, storeId:null); ... DB::rollBack(); ..."
Result: totalTaxamount=5 (5% VAT on $100, tax id 3) — same shape/values as pre-fix expectation.
OrderTax row 98 written by the nested savepoint DURING the transaction (confirms writes still happen).
After our own outer DB::rollBack(): OrderTax row 98 count = 0 (confirms nested savepoint correctly
unwinds when the ambient/outer transaction rolls back — no orphaned writes, DB restored to pre-test state).
